/Title (This report answers all five questions of Lab 1 \(50 marks\). A transparent keyword-based classifier labels each message as Safe, Phishing, Malware or Ransomware, assigns a risk level and recommended action, and is evaluated on the full dataset. All outputs below come from an actual run of the code shown \(Python, pandas, scikit-learn\).)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 652 0 R
/Next 712 0 R
>>
endobj
712 0 obj
<<
/Title (Note on the dataset: the faculty file simple_cyber_messages.csv was not supplied, so I created a 28-message sanitized dataset in the same format \(message_id, message, correct_category\): 10 Safe, 7 Phishing, 6 Malware and 5 Ransomware. The first ten messages follow the important-word hints in the manual. No real links or files are used. If you receive the faculty CSV, run the same code on it and update the numbers; the manual expects 28 of 28 correct on its own file.)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 652 0 R
/Prev 711 0 R
